{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1073791-pantheon-question","id":1073791,"title":"Pantheon Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-05T10:34:03-07:00","id":1073791,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Pantheon Question","content":"I'm curious. If there a Pantheon that claims Puerto Rico? Either the Aztecs or the Loa?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2526-aazen","name":"Aazen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T10:48:39-07:00","id":1073797,"title":"","content":"Depends on if you want an already established pantheon or not. If it already needs to be in the game, the Loa would be your closest fit. The island really should be part of the Zemi, the pantheon for the native Taino people of the Greater Antilles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12989-center-of-all","name":"Center-of-All","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T10:53:14-07:00","id":1073798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Center-of-All</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1073791-pantheon-question?p=1073797#post1073797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on if you want an already established pantheon or not. If it already needs to be in the game, the Loa would be your closest fit. The island really should be part of the Zemi, the pantheon for the native Taino people of the Greater Antilles.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Zemi? Where can I find out more about them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2526-aazen","name":"Aazen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T11:56:23-07:00","id":1073813,"title":"","content":"Talking about the pantheons that belong the manual i think that puerto rico could be a &quot;divided&quot; land between Greeks (for columbus) and azlanti","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T13:28:03-07:00","id":1073859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1073791-pantheon-question?p=1073813#post1073813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking about the pantheons that belong the manual i think that puerto rico could be a &quot;divided&quot; land between Greeks (for columbus) and azlanti</div> </div> </div> </div>What does an Italian Catholic have to do with the Theoi?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T14:39:32-07:00","id":1073887,"title":"","content":"I'd really like to see the Zemi included at some point, but I'm concerned that they're too obscure even for this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T14:41:26-07:00","id":1073889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1073791-pantheon-question?p=1073887#post1073887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd really like to see the Zemi included at some point, but I'm concerned that they're too obscure even for this game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the devs have spoken about the Guarani gods, nothing is too niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T15:36:43-07:00","id":1073909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1073791-pantheon-question?p=1073859#post1073859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What does an Italian Catholic have to do with the Theoi?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Columbus was a traveler, a curious mind, almost a scientific mind not such a great catholic <br /> <br /> What i mean is: He's an italian traveler blessed by the greek/roman gods, pushed to the west to expand the area of influence of the pantheon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T17:28:58-07:00","id":1073939,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I'm now imagining a bunch of native Puerto Rican Heroes, each from different pantheons, who argue and compete over who should be the island's official champion. <br /> <br /> <br /> An interesting (to me, at least) aside about Columbus; Orson Scott Card's Pastwatch: The Redemption of Christopher Columbus posited that his original destiny was to rally and lead a new Crusade against the Ottoman Turks in the wake of the fall of Constantinople, until time travelers meddled in order to prevent the global dominance of a brutal Tlaxcalan empire. In Scion, I have this image of said plot being the result of some sort of power struggle between the Greek, Aztec and one or more other pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T19:51:21-07:00","id":1073991,"title":"","content":"The \u00d2r\u00ecsh\u00e0 have a lot of worshippers in Puerto Rican Lukum\u00ed and Palo. If we had more wordcount, we could probably add an Igbo Pantheon to the Afro-Atlantic confederation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T23:31:17-07:00","id":1074029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aazen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1073791-pantheon-question?p=1073798#post1073798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Zemi? Where can I find out more about them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I pretty much have no idea, but I looked around a bit, and there were a lot of good critiques for this book? <a href=\"https://books.google.de/books?id=7S1qAAAAMAAJ&amp;q=Cave+of+the+Jagua+:+the+mythological+world+of+the+Ta%C3%ADnos&amp;dq=Cave+of+the+Jagua+:+the+mythological+world+of+the+Ta%C3%ADnos&amp;hl=de&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0ahUKEwjp09bJmo_TAhUJB8AKHSQPAdgQ6AEIHTAA\" target=\"_blank\">https://books.google.de/books?id=7S1...QPAdgQ6AEIHTAA</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T09:22:45-07:00","id":1077019,"title":"","content":"Well. That's an idea for a chronicle:<br /> <br /> Puerto Rico is the battleground for the azlanti, Greeks, and loa as they duke it out for the territory because the oracles say a scion will kill a Titian there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2526-aazen","name":"Aazen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T20:03:33-07:00","id":1078725,"title":"","content":"If you ever pass through Manhattan and you visit the 6 train stop at 110th Street and Lexington Avenue, you'll see a set of four mosaics on the walls entitled &quot;Sabado en la Ciento Diez&quot; (&quot;Saturday on 110th Street&quot;), by Puerto Rican artist Manuel Vega. Two of the mosaics depict \u1e62\u00e0ng\u00f3 and Yem\u1ecdja of the \u00d2r\u00ec\u1e63\u00e0 (or as they call them in PR, Chang\u00f3 and Yemay\u00e1 of the Orich\u00e1s).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T17:19:09-07:00","id":1079125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1073791-pantheon-question?p=1078725#post1078725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you ever pass through Manhattan and you visit the 6 train stop at 110th Street and Lexington Avenue, you'll see a set of four mosaics on the walls entitled &quot;Sabado en la Ciento Diez&quot; (&quot;Saturday on 110th Street&quot;), by Puerto Rican artist Manuel Vega. Two of the mosaics depict \u1e62\u00e0ng\u00f3 and Yem\u1ecdja of the \u00d2r\u00ec\u1e63\u00e0 (or as they call them in PR, Chang\u00f3 and Yemay\u00e1 of the Orich\u00e1s).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sorry. I'm not familiar with them. What pantheon are they and where can I find them, crunch wise? Beautiful Mural though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2526-aazen","name":"Aazen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T17:53:28-07:00","id":1079134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aazen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1073791-pantheon-question?p=1079125#post1079125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry. I'm not familiar with them. What pantheon are they and where can I find them, crunch wise? Beautiful Mural though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Orisha are the Pantheon of the Yoruban people of modern day Nigeria, believe sort of central-coastal area. In the crook of the nation's bend. The Orisha form the vast bulk of the Loa, transitioning across the sea, picking up some Deities from neighboring people, fracturing their Deity named Eshu into Kalfu and Legba, as well as the entirely new face of Baron Samedi who has no known roots in pre-Triangle Trade Africa.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:12:47-07:00","id":1083558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1073791-pantheon-question?p=1079134#post1079134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Orisha are the Pantheon of the Yoruban people of modern day Nigeria, believe sort of central-coastal area. In the crook of the nation's bend. The Orisha form the vast bulk of the Loa, transitioning across the sea, picking up some Deities from neighboring people, fracturing their Deity named Eshu into Kalfu and Legba, as well as the entirely new face of Baron Samedi who has no known roots in pre-Triangle Trade Africa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very close! The Loa are loosely organized into &quot;nasyons&quot; representing West African ethnic groups. The largest of these is the Rada nasyon, derived from a pantheon called the Vodun whom the Ewe and Fon people of Dahomey (in modern-day Benin) worshipped. Other nasyons include the Ibo (Igbo), Kongo (Angolan etc.), and Petro (peculiar to Haiti). The Nago nasyon, which corresponds to the Yor\u00f9b\u00e1, is relatively small, sometimes considered a subset of the Petro; from this fact we can surmise that a smaller proportion of Yor\u00f9b\u00e1 captives wound up in Haiti than in Cuba, Puerto Rico, Trinidad, or Brazil. The best-known Nago Loa are Ogou and his various forms, some of which represent other Yor\u00f9b\u00e1 \u00d2r\u00ecsh\u00e0: Ogou Shango combines the \u00d2r\u00ecsh\u00e0 \u00d2g\u00fan and Sh\u00e0ng\u00f3, Ogou Bhathalah combines \u00d2g\u00fan and Ob\u00e0t\u00e1l\u00e1, etc. That said, the geographic proximity of Yor\u00f9b\u00e1land and Dahomey means there are some pretty clear correspondences between \u00d2r\u00ecsh\u00e0 figures and Vodun ones even in their African forms: both groups have sacred twins and rainbow serpents, for example. It's pretty common for Afro-Atlantic religious practitioners today to draw associations pretty freely between figures from different traditions: for example, &quot;\u00d2shun is the same as Ezili Freda&quot; is a pretty common casual statement you'll hear from Lukum\u00ed or voodoo practitioners, even though strictly speaking there are many differences between them.<br /> <br /> The \u00d2r\u00ecsh\u00e0 will appear in <i>Scion: Hero.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T14:35:12-07:00","id":1083693,"title":"","content":"Are Erzulie Freda and Erzulie Dantour two different goddesses (perhaps twins?) or two Mantles of the same goddess in different nasyons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T21:57:47-07:00","id":1083837,"title":"","content":"I consider them completely different. Freda's Rada, Dantor's Petro, and they don't act even remotely like one another. I've seen different Ogou possess multiple people in the same room, and they act similar (same dance steps, same attitude, etc.), but Freda and Dantor don't move, dance, or interact similarly. Freda loads up on scarves and jewelry and is polite, flirty, and wry; Dantor doesn't even/can't even talk, and she's blunt, direct, and even a little rude. Their name and gender are the only thing they have in common.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T23:14:15-07:00","id":1083872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1073791-pantheon-question?p=1083837#post1083837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I consider them completely different. Freda's Rada, Dantor's Petro, and they don't act even remotely like one another. I've seen different Ogou possess multiple people in the same room, and they act similar (same dance steps, same attitude, etc.), but Freda and Dantor don't move, dance, or interact similarly. Freda loads up on scarves and jewelry and is polite, flirty, and wry; Dantor doesn't even/can't even talk, and she's blunt, direct, and even a little rude. Their name and gender are the only thing they have in common.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *nods* I was just wondering as they were explained to me as being complementary opposites, the opposing Rada and Petwo takes on the domain of passion and relationships. But I admit my first hand knowledge is limited at nonexistent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 04-26-2017, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T19:49:54-07:00","id":1084268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1073791-pantheon-question?p=1083872#post1083872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*nods* I was just wondering as they explained to me as being complementary opposites, the opposing Rada and Petwo takes on the domain of passion and relationships. But I admit my first hand knowledge is limited at nonexistent.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely a legit and common interpretation; it just isn't that descriptive, practically speaking. In Scion terms they're gonna be separate principals. But &quot;Freda and Danto are opposite sides of the same coin&quot; isn't, like, an offensive statement or anything, and at least from a scholarly perspective it's an assertion worth considering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T03:17:36-07:00","id":1084395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1073791-pantheon-question?p=1084268#post1084268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It